fB-cuAuQh--F_ajkiO2c4PkYf1IKufTVFLyPduCUC9g5ruKbtTUscDRhAWhulqVq8CgnAZX8gv7rG4uALuSR99QxM_ORDGb1Xhlm_VJqrcJzxQxliF9LhQfjKJEGli2eNNQJicCeHICFTto-TAA7ubhgdcRt4jpFkW2YOiBDdgR08Rp7bhHQQs6y_1_w9HH0-i4Oz1p3buu_6swZGWnPp-ldmMXFevI56sgfIkw_xeMUI97ts3dlotf7-jvscxtS9kzbxsLuwQ3OECqDa-nR181x9PagfCur8J-fUsVWDfTXL4XqlSsN3menyjAjbYZDTjiUKgsMrX4lEeMpgr2PjOlv0ov2-99GhOxpYx8hPhr6ZrOsdWZcL8aisIc9JllPO809zks7zFzUvtxnwJNLFTBjkJ-90FPUkFpwlO66wN8LhTv9zcMbONIuJwHUxWHHIyumJ1iobQ18tdVCclkozWfZSvW62zwlSCF5Lf"},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_04de6b92baab60ea016adb477c310c81919b7fa617bf417e15","call_id":"call_3e3162942c5a4b6fb1db79146918a255","name":"check_artifact","arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"base_candidate\\\":45,\\\"patches\\\":[{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/1/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary t>0, set J=[t/2,3t/2], and choose compact C from H003 so u(x,s)=q for every x∉C and s∈J. To prove Lebesgue measure finite on every compact, fix arbitrary compact K⊂ℝⁿ. By M016, K is bounded. If K is empty, it is contained in every closed ball. Otherwise choose x₀∈K; boundedness supplies a finite L≥0 such that ‖x−x₀‖≤L for every x∈K. Set R₀=‖x₀‖+L+1; the triangle inequality gives ‖x‖≤R₀ for every x∈K. In either case obtain F001: ∃R₀>0, ∀x∈K, ‖x‖≤R₀. This proves the witness basis for the next paragraph.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/1/argument/1/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Choose R₀ using F001 and define Q=∏_{i=1}^n[-R₀,R₀]. Each coordinate has absolute value at most ‖x‖, hence K⊆Q. The coordinate Lebesgue measure is sigma-finite: the countable measurable intervals [-k,k] cover ℝ and each has finite measure by M014, so they are a countable finite-measure cover. M013 and M014 then give μ(Q)=∏_{i=1}^n μ([-R₀,R₀])=(2R₀)^n<∞. Apply M018 to the compact K in the Hausdorff Euclidean space to conclude K is closed and hence Borel measurable; monotonicity yields μ(K)≤μ(Q)<∞. As K was arbitrary, Lebesgue measure is finite on compact sets. The Borel measurable structure on ℝⁿ is the σ-algebra generated by Euclidean opens, so opens are measurable. Joint smoothness and u=q on the open spatial complement of C throughout J imply all first spatial and time derivatives, and the second and mixed derivatives entering e_t, vanish outside C. Thus e(·,t) is continuous with compact support in C. Apply M001 to conclude e(·,t) is integrable. The same smoothness/support argument shows u_t(·,s), u_{x_j}(·,s), e(·,s), and e_t(·,s) are continuous and vanish off C for each s∈J and j=1,…,n. This proves the claimed output for arbitrary t>0.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/1/applications/2/hypothesis_checks/1\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Each ℝ coordinate with Lebesgue measure is sigma-finite because the countable intervals [−k,k] cover ℝ and M014 gives finite measure for each.\\\"}]}\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additi